cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "FaultLine: a from-scratch joint telemetry-text sequence model for wind-turbine event risk, built and evaluated as a pre-registered study"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Erniyazov
    given-names: Sarvarbek
    affiliation: "Chonnam National University"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Sarvarbek-Erniyazov/FaultLine"
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-09-27"
abstract: >-
  A decoder-only transformer written from scratch over a joint vocabulary of byte-level BPE
  text tokens and per-channel quantile-bin telemetry tokens, pretrained at 50M tokens per arm
  on one 8 GB GPU and evaluated as a pre-registered study of wind-turbine SCADA event risk
  (will a fault event start in the next 24 hours). Every evaluation rule was committed before
  the run it governs. The experimental programme closed on 2026-09-20. Site shift gave two
  pre-registered negatives (Hill of Towie and CARE not evaluable). Telemetry-only, the
  sequence model is at parity with an order-blind bag of tokens. The text-aware joint
  read-out beat the telemetry-only model on the registered label (H1' supported) but is
  inconclusive under the anemometer-excluded variant, and is level with a classifier that
  counts status strings. Graceful degradation under channel loss was not established (H2
  inconclusive), and the probabilities under-read the test-period event rate, so they are
  rankings, not risks. In exploratory analysis after closure, a time-since-last-fault
  baseline beat the model.
keywords:
  - sequence modeling
  - selective prediction
  - wind energy
  - SCADA
